{"kind":"propose","text":"Proposed design: compose the approved bounded-status projection with the signed-checkpoint read path; do not build a third cache. Problem split. At durable depth 616, local gs status took 57.97 seconds (21.38 user, 28.11 system, 24.9 MB max RSS). The default human result was 19,142 bytes and 247 lines. Resident full JSON was 1,163,853 bytes: 486 statements, 616 decisions, and 616 provenance entries. Source inspection shows cold reconstruction launches several Git subprocesses per event for commit signature, parent, envelope, tree, payload-shape, payload, and attachment checks; rendering 19 KB is not the latency cause, while full serialization and transport are a separate linear-growth cost. Candidate evidence. The unmerged signed-checkpoint repair at efd228ebface98b2a833793f9fbe209f5962610b took 70.96 seconds for the initial cold audit plus checkpoint, then 0.20 seconds for a fresh exact-head one-shot status, about 290x faster; after a small live tail it took 0.77 seconds. Its documented depth-1000 case with a 232-event tail takes 20.29 seconds, so exact-head, small-tail, worst-cadence-tail, and no-checkpoint fallback must remain separate measurements. Read path. First, when the caller explicitly supplies --server, gs requests a new bounded resident-summary endpoint rather than downloading the complete projection. It accepts no redirects, only loopback, caps response bytes and elapsed time, and requires returned genesis and head to match the local config and current sequence ref; mismatch or failure falls back locally and is never labeled current. No automatic port discovery is added. Second, local status uses Task 2g.1 signed checkpoints and verifies only the descendant tail. It adds no status-specific cache or trust format. Missing, corrupt, wrong-profile, wrong-genesis, oversized, or non-descendant checkpoints retain the existing full cryptographic audit fallback. gs verify never uses the shortcut. A fallback lasting more than one second prints one plain progress line to stderr so a real audit is slow but not silent. View. Move the already approved bounded actor-view logic from task/status-projection into one internal status-view package shared by MCP, service, and CLI, preserving its caps, authority-role retention, verdict distinctions, and honest skipped counters. Add a global human view in the same package. Default gs status prints frontier/source and total counts, then newest-first bounded groups: actionable requested/promised/reported commitments; unresolved attention such as stale, reneged, or cancelled commitments; current and stale artifacts; and non-effective attempts. Every group keeps at most 20, caps request text at 240 bytes, resolves actor fingerprints to names, and prints X of N whenever truncated. Satisfied and withdrawn history is counted but not listed by default. gs status --all preserves the existing complete Markdown tables. gs status --json preserves the existing complete Snapshot JSON and schema. With --server, default text is the bounded live summary while --all or --json requests the complete existing /v0/status shape. The browser and /v0/status remain complete. Acceptance. A synthetic projection with 10,000 entries in every growth dimension keeps default text and resident-summary JSON below 32 KiB, each list at 20, every omitted count exact, and doubling history changes only totals rather than row count. Full text and JSON continue to contain every entry. On this live workroom at depth at least 616, three separate exact-head checkpointed invocations have median \u003c=500 ms and a \u003c=10-event tail completes \u003c=2 seconds; the performance fixture also proves prefix verification uses a bounded number of Git processes plus work proportional to the tail, not one subprocess family per cached event. A warm depth-20k resident summary has \u003c=500 ms p99 end to end and \u003c=64 KiB response. Corrupt, stale, foreign, oversized, redirecting, slow, and moving-head resident/checkpoint cases all select the honest local/full fallback and never return a false-current summary. Tests pin each cap and each trust guard by mutation, preserve full-mode golden output, and pass vet, test, race, build, and diff checks. Dependencies and sequencing. Merge only independently approved exact heads for task/status-projection ae601b52b6842ed8b282de6f9d53ac74b29125a4 and Task 2g.1 checkpoint after its pending re-review. After both are on main, implement this proposal in task/status-fast-usable with a Rests-On trailer naming this ratified proposal, publish an exact artifact/report, obtain independent exact-head approval, and merge only that approval. No implementation begins before ratification.","body":{"decision":"explicit resident summary, then signed checkpoint plus tail, then honest full audit; bounded default, --all full text, --json full snapshot","dependencies":"status-projection ae601b52b6842ed8b282de6f9d53ac74b29125a4 approved but unmerged; checkpoint efd228ebface98b2a833793f9fbe209f5962610b pending re-review","measurements":"depth616 local 57.97s and 19142B; resident full 1163853B; checkpoint first 70.96s, reuse 0.20s, small-tail 0.77s"}}